 The Hive table schema is kept in sync with the Iceberg table. If an outside source (Impala/Spark/Java API/etc)
 changes the schema, the Hive table immediately reflects the changes. You alter the table schema using Hive commands:
 
+!!! info
+    Hive Metastore (HMS) compatibility can affect Iceberg schema-evolution operations. Some operations, such as
+    renaming a column, changing a column type, or reordering columns, may be constrained by the HMS version in use.
+    Use a supported HMS version (Hive 2.3.10 or 3.1.3 or later, as described in the
+    [Global Hive catalog](#global-hive-catalog) section) to avoid unexpected limitations.
+
